Regarding the April 28, 2025, general election: 
a) number of mail-in ballots requested by electors; 
b) number of mail-in ballots forwarded to electors as requested; 
c) number of mail-in ballots forwarded to electors, the number that left Elections Canada on the following days: April 21st, April 22nd, April 23rd, April 24th, April 25th, April 26th and April 27th; 
d) number of mail-in ballots returned and counted on April 28th; 
e) number of mail-in ballots received past Elections Canada's deadline that went uncounted.

Regarding the April 28, 2025, general election: 
a) number of mail-in ballots requested by electors; 
b) number of mail-in ballots forwarded to electors as requested; 
c) of the number identified in (b), the number mailed from Elections Canada on April 21st, the number mailed on April 22nd, the number mailed on April 23rd, the number mailed on April 24th, the number mailed on April 25th, the number mailed on April 26th and the number mailed on April 27th; 
d) total number of completed mail-in ballots returned by electors past Elections Canada's deadline that went uncounted.

For the period from October 1st 2019 to July 12th 2025, relating to collections of audio recordings and textual material which contain any of the following:
- Aboriginal (Indigenous, First Nations, Métis, Inuit) music played upon a Violin/Fiddle;
- Métis dance;
- Métis song or music using other instruments;

We request digital/digitised copies of relevant policy documents (please include both draft and final versions):
- Museum policies affecting any barriers to access for these collections.
- Museum policies around Indigenous access to collections of Indigenous material in the collections (without repatriation). 
- Museum policies regarding repatriation.
- All Museum policies, protocols and guidelines related to UNDRIP that inform access to and repatriation from Indigenous collections.

Please include both policies in effect and policies under development.

