The development is a high-rise, 25-storey building located at the northeast quadrant of the Harwood Ave South/Achilles Rd intersection, in proximity to the rail tracks in the Town of Ajax, approximately 1.6 km east of the Ajax Go Train Station (For your reference, please see the attached map).

As such, it would be highly appreciated if we could receive the following information: 
•Current number of VIA trains operating per day;
•Number and configuration of VIA locomotives per train;
•Weight of VIA locomotives along this section of track;
•Design speed of VIA trains along this section of track;
•Any other relevant information VIA may be able to share in the context of rail safety and land use planning adjacent to the corrido

It is understood that both the GO Trains and VIA Rail Trains share the rail segment ranging from Union Station to the Pickering Junction (just west of Pickering GO Station).

As such, it would be highly appreciated if we could receive the following information: 
•Current number of VIA trains operating per day;
•Number and configuration of VIA locomotives per train;
•Weight of VIA locomotives along this section of track;
•Design speed of VIA trains along this section of track;
•Any other relevant information VIA may be able to share in the context of rail safety and land use planning adjacent to the corridor.

All documents containing the results of consultations conducted for the purposes of developing the “Employment and Social Development Canada 3-year accessibility plan – 2022” including:    
1) the summary report and annexes from the employee and manager engagement sessions held by the ESDC Accessibility Office between August and October 2020;    
2) interview notes and results from virtual focus groups conducted between July and December 2021 during the “Service Channel Access Consultation”   
3) results and notes from interviews conducted by outreach officers with community organizations regarding barriers to service from 2018 onwards, except the raw data;   
4) survey results from front-line staff, except the raw data;   
6) all responses from the 916 participants who identified as having a disability in the 2020 to 2021 Service Canada Client Experience (CX) Survey

